{
  "Daniel.2.16.8-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.12, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 2:16.8</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 2:16.8</h1>\n  <h2>Note possible dagesh in the first nun and weak dot in tsere under the tav.  Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.12/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text is in good condition near this word. A reddish blob appears in nun; it is poorly formed and ill-positioned, compared to the dagesh in the tav. The blob will not be transcribed as a dagesh. The leading dot in the tsere under the tav is reddish and small but well-formed and well positioned. It will remain a tsere.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no dagesh in the nun and a tsere under the tav.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.12-1\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.12-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.2.45.12-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.12, number: 4 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 2:45.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 2:45.12</h1>\n  <h2>Segol under the dalet has a weak lower dot. Add a note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.12/4-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The dot below the tsere is reddish and light; however, it is well-sized and well-positioned. The text does not have many extraneous dots near this word. The vowel will continue as  segol.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a tsere under the dalet.  BHLA has a segol under the dalet with a '?' in parentheses.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.12-4\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.12-4</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.2.9.13-q.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.04.15, number: 38 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 2:9.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 2:9.13</h1>\n  <h2>Remove unsupported dagesh from dalet in qere word. Add note 'q'. [הִזְדְּמִנְתּוּן֙]</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.04.15/38-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The qere word in the left margin, הזדמנתון, has a dalet between the zayin and mem. The ketiv body text shown in the image has no dalet, but has two adjacent shevas under the zayin. No dagesh is available in the ketiv body text to support a dagesh in the dalet.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a dagesh in the dalet, הִזְדְּמִנְתּוּן֙, in the qere word.  BHLA has no entry for this word in the verse; however, it has an entry for word 24.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.04.15-38\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.04.15-38</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?q\">All \"UXLC differs from the conventional word for the qere.\" ('q') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.3.15.12-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 16 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 3:15.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 3:15.12</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/16-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir vav. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  (This word contains no vav; it has a holam on the next-to-last letter, resh.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  See change 2024.07.11 - 1 which follows.) </p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair; the qere form has no yod after the qof and no vav.  \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  BHLA has an entry for this verse; the entry is for word 38 (דֵּ֥י), not this word. (Word 38 agrees with BHLA)</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-16\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-16</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.3.21.6-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 17 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 3:21.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 3:21.6</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod) Add note 't' for ambiguity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/17-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is in the right margin; it is a yatir yod. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe word has 2 yods; neither is vowelized. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe first yod in the word will be noted as a yatir here. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tA note 't' will be added to reflect this ambiguity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere has a single unvowelized, unaccented yod after the shin. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-17\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-17</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.3.21.6-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 17 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 3:21.6</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 3:21.6</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod) Add note 't' for ambiguity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/17-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is in the right margin; it is a yatir yod. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe word has 2 yods; neither is vowelized. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tThe first yod in the word will be noted as a yatir here. \n\t\t\t\t\t\tA note 't' will be added to reflect this ambiguity.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere has a single unvowelized, unaccented yod after the shin. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-17\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-17</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.3.28.23-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 18 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 3:28.23</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 3:28.23</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/18-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir marking for this word is the left margin; it is a yatir yod. A raised yod appears between the mem and the he.</p>\n  <p>BHL has  a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere form has no yod between the mem and the he.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-18\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-18</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.4.14.17-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 19 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 4:14.17</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 4:14.17</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir vav)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/19-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The line has two markings in the left margin but no Masorah circles. The first marking is a qere form indicating that a he follows an aleph. This applies to preceding  words 14 and 15. The second marking is a yatir vav. Two vavs appear on the line; the one in word 16 is vowelized with a dagesh acting as a shuruq. Hence, this marking must be for word 17.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere form has no vav. BHL also agrees with the qere/ketiv pair in words 14 and 15. BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-19\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-19</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.5.10.19-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.01, number: 2 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 5:10.19</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 5:10.19</h1>\n  <h2>Add note 't' to preceding change: 2024.07.01 - 1 for ambiquity.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.01/2-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.01/2b-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img2>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <b>\n        <center>Expanded view of text in area of word.</center>\n        </b>\n        <p>\n        </p>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The LC word contains two yods: one before and one after the second vav. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  The second yod is broken and squeezed between the second vav and the final kaf. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  The right margin of the text contains the note \"יתיר י  (yatir yod)\" for the LC word;\n\t\t\t\t\t\t      hence, the LC word should be represented by a qere/ketiv pair.\n \t\t\t\t\t\t  In the preceding change, 2024.07.01 - 1, \n \t\t\t\t\t\t      the letters from the LC text were placed in the preceding ketiv word (k tag) \n \t\t\t\t\t\t          and the qere (q tag) was placed in this word.    \n                          The resulting qere/ketiv pair is found in the BHL, MAM, and JPS Tanach 1999; \n                             however, it is not in WLC 4.20. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t  Because neither the margin note nor the Masora dot specifies which yod is superfluous,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t      this  transcription note 't' will be added to this word.\n                    </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.01-2\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.01-2</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.5.10.19-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 20 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 5:10.19</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 5:10.19</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/20-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The yatir note is in the right margin; it is a yatir yod. The first word on the line has a Masorah circle and two unvowelized and unaccented yods. The second of these yods, between the vav and final kaf, is broken. The 'y' note will be added to the second yod. This word is not represented by a qere/ketiv pair in previous versions of the UXLC or in WLC 4.20.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere form has a single yod after the zayin.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-20\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-20</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.5.20.12-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2022.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2022.07.29, number: 1 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 5:20.12</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 5:20.12</h1>\n  <h2>Remove dagesh from vav. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/images/2022.07.29/1-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n                     Though well-positioned, the dagesh on the vav is very faint compared to other dots on the word.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n                     The vocalization with the dagesh didn't make sense here.\n               </p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Asael Reiter</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes/2022.10.19 - Changes.xml?2022.07.29-1\">2022.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2022.07.29-1</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.5.23.13-y.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2024.07.08, number: 21 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 5:23.13</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 5:23.13</h1>\n  <h2>Add transcription note 'y' to yatir ketiv word. (yatir yod)</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/images/2024.07.08/21-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>This line has 3 markings: a qere marking for the first word in the right margin that lacks a Masorah cirle and a qere marking in the left for the second word, as indicated by the Masorah cirle. The third word has a Masorah circle and has a yatir yod marking.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a qere/ketiv pair for this word; the qere forn has no yod betweeb the nun and final kaf.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>CVK</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes/2024.10.19 - Changes.xml?2024.07.08-21\">2024.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2024.07.08-21</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?y\">All \"Yatir: The preceding Hebrew letter is \"superfluous\".\" ('y') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.6.27.27-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.12, number: 14 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 6:27.27</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 6:27.27</h1>\n  <h2>Ambiguous vowel under the bet. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.12/14-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text quality is poor. The vowel under the bet is ambiguous and might be a qamats.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a patah under the bet.  BHLA has no entry for this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.12-14\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.12-14</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Daniel.7.19.3-t.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2024.04.01 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.12, number: 16 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Daniel 7:19.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Daniel 7:19.3</h1>\n  <h2>Examine accent over bet. Add note 't'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/images/2023.09.12/16-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The text is of poor quality. The upper dot of the current zaqef-qatan is weak, but well-positioned. The lower dot is low for a revia.</p>\n  <p>BHL has a zaqef-qatan over the bet.  BHLA has no entry for this word in this verse.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes/2024.04.01 - Changes.xml?2023.09.12-16\">2024.04.01 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.12-16</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>"
}
